        "evidence": [
          {
            "end": 1477,
            "passage_index": 1,
            "quote": "WT VCL completely rescues actin ring formation and bone resorption, as does VCL(P878A), which is incapable of interacting with Arp2/3. As expected, deletion of the VCL tail domain (VCL(1-880)), which binds actin, does not normalize VCL(-/-) osteoclasts. The same is true regarding VCL(I997A), which also prevents VCL/actin binding, and VCL(A50I) and VCL(811-1066), both of which arrest talin association. Thus, VCL binding talin, but not Arp2/3, is critical for osteoclast function, and its selective inhibition retards physiological bone loss.",
            "start": 933
          }
        ],
